      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8ec19663",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: the_most_confusing_moments; hasOverallIntent: non-toxic-humor; overall-intent-description: The image features a close-up of a bulldog with an exaggerated, open-mouthed expression, often interpreted as a 'confused' or 'dumb' look. The text 'the most confusing moments' is overlaid, creating a humorous juxtaposition. The meme's intent is to evoke laughter by anthropomorphizing the dog's expression as a relatable human experience of confusion. There is no toxicity, harmful content, or disparaging stereotype present. The humor is derived from the visual absurdity and the relatable human emotion of confusion, not from targeting any group or individual based on protected characteristics. The bulldog's appearance is used as a visual metaphor for bewilderment, not as a caricature of any marginalized group.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
