      "instance_name": "confused_bulldog_stereotype",
      "label": "Confused Bulldog Stereotype",
      "description": "The bulldog's exaggerated, open-mouthed expression is culturally interpreted as a visual metaphor for confusion or 'dumbness'. This anthropomorphism relies on the real-world stereotype that bulldogs are unintelligent or slow-witted, which is then humorously applied to human experiences of confusion. The meme leverages this pre-existing visual trope to create relatable humor.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
